Subject: Make ICU converter alignment, TOC bounds, timezone, and data generation Fil-C safe
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: ucnv_clone() aligns a stack buffer pointer via integer reinterpret_cast (stripping Fil-C capability metadata), ICU's data builder emits raw ELF/assembly object files that cannot link under Fil-C, and uprv_timezone()'s localtime/mktime fallback is fragile under Fil-C. Re-deriving the aligned pointer with zmkptr(), bounding TOC tables, and disabling assembly/object data emission keeps ICU4C 79.1 fully capability-safe.
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de02b42

